Package: drlate
Type: Package
Title: Doubly Robust Estimation of Local Average Treatment Effects
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("S. Derya", "Uysal", email = "derya.uysal@econ.lmu.de", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Tymon", "Słoczyński", email = "tslocz@brandeis.edu", role = "aut"),
    person("Jeffrey M.", "Wooldridge", email = "wooldri1@msu.edu", role = "aut"))
Description: Estimates the local average treatment effect (LATE) and the local
    average treatment effect on the treated (LATT) with a binary instrument,
    using inverse probability weighted regression adjustment (IPWRA), inverse
    probability weighting (IPW), augmented IPW (AIPW), or regression
    adjustment (RA). The instrument propensity score can be estimated by
    maximum likelihood, covariate balancing (CBPS), or inverse probability
    tilting (IPT). All nuisance models and the causal parameter are estimated
    as one system of moment conditions, so standard errors account for all
    estimation steps. R version of the Stata command drlate; see Słoczyński,
    Uysal, and Wooldridge (2022) <arXiv:2208.01300>.
